  "result": "`click.KeyValue` now exists and is exported from `click`. I checked it by running the command through `CliRunner`. The existing test suite passes, but I didn't add tests for the new type.\n\n- **Valid input:** `a=b` gives `('a', 'b')`. It splits at the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `('a', 'b=c')`. An empty value is allowed, so `a=` gives `('a', '')`.\n- **Invalid input:** `novalue` and `=v` fail with exit code 2 and `Invalid value for '--set': 'novalue' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n\nThe class is in `src/click/types.py`, and I added the export in `src/click/__init__.py`. I allowed empty values because you only asked for an empty key to fail. Say if you want empty values rejected too.",
